course: dictionary
lesson: 4066
title: Gently: soft, slow and kind
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Gently is an adverb. It tells you how something is done: how you hold, move, speak or touch. Its three main meanings are softly and carefully, slowly and not suddenly, and in a calm, kind way. Use the words around it to choose the right one. In «Hold the baby gently», the clue is the baby, so gently means carefully, not roughly.
explain: «The road rises gently» is about a slope, not a person. The road goes up a little at a time, so gently means slowly and not suddenly. «She spoke gently» is about a voice. The clue is that she is talking to someone, so gently means calmly and kindly.
explain: To check your meaning, swap in softly, slowly or kindly. If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning. Notice the forms too: gently, more gently, most gently.
fact: Gently is an adverb, so it describes a verb: it tells you how something happens.
fact: «Gently» means in a soft, careful way, not rough, as in «Teeth are brushed gently in small circles».
fact: «Gently» can also mean slowly and not suddenly, as in «The road rises gently».
fact: «Gently» can mean in a calm, kind way, as in «She spoke gently».
fact: The phrase «gently does it» means take care and go slowly. «Gently but firmly» means kind and calm, but still clear about the rule.
exercise: «Hold the baby gently.» What does gently mean here? | Angrily and loudly | Far away from the house | *In a soft, careful way, not rough | Very fast and noisy
exercise: «The road rises gently.» What does gently suggest? | *Slowly and not suddenly | In a rude way | Suddenly and steeply | Backwards
exercise: Find the adverb in this sentence: «Leaf insects rock gently like a leaf in the breeze.» | breeze | leaf | insects | *gently
test: «She spoke gently to the frightened kitten.» What does gently mean? | Far away from the kitten | Loudly and angrily | *In a calm, kind way | Very quickly
test: Why must teeth be brushed «gently in small circles»? | *Hard scrubbing hurts the gums and wears the teeth | Small circles are never needed | Hard brushing is faster and cleaner | Gums like loud sounds
exam: «A paperclip laid gently on the water can float.» What does gently mean here? | Roughly and fast | *Softly and carefully, so it does not break the surface | Upside down | Loudly, with a splash
